WEBVTT
NOTE SYNC_TYPE: HUMAN_VERIFIED
NOTE Track: 1-04 - The DeMarco Decree
NOTE Artist: The Paper Wall
NOTE Album: 2000: Guiding Stars

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.800
[Instrumental Intro: Flute & Rock Band]

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.600
Another Monday, bells are ringing loud

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.900
Lost inside a noisy, shuffling crowd

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.500
There's Josh Riley, king of the obscene

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.900
Making another ugly little scene

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.400
He thinks he's tough, he thinks he's cool

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.988
Breaking every single golden rule

00:00:48.028 --> 00:00:51.500
But here she comes, the final word

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.200
The quiet calm before the storm is heard

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.600
And the DeMarco Decree comes raining down

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.000
On the baddest, saddest bully in this town

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.500
Another week of picking up the trash

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.900
Another lesson in a brilliant flash

00:01:08.997 --> 00:01:11.200
And I catch your eye across the floor

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.361
We've seen this happen here before

00:01:18.489 --> 00:01:22.000
He doesn't learn, he never will

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.400
He's standing on the same old hill

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.900
Of pointless pride and cheap-shot lies

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.552
Right there before our watching eyes

00:01:32.372 --> 00:01:35.800
But justice here is swift and true

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.200
For me and especially for you

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.800
The gavel falls, the sentence read

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:49.500
The words that fill us both with dread... are not for us

